    <data name="IntroBody" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>{0} landing pages for {0} kinds of business, each one ready to become yours. This tour opens a few of them and points out what comes built in.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="ModesTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Launched, or not yet</value>
    </data>
    <data name="ModesBody" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>A sample counts as launched once one of its apps is live, and then it links to the stores. Until then, it collects a waitlist.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="RatingTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>{0}, an online shop</value>
    </data>
    <data name="RatingBody" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Its App Store listing is read live from Apple and kept on the server for a while: the rating once there are enough of them, the latest version until then. The badges list only the stores the app is in.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="ChatTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>An assistant that knows the business</value>
    </data>
    <data name="ChatBody" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>It answers from {0}'s own facts, in the visitor's language. Its code downloads only when someone opens it.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="WaitlistTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>{0}, before its launch</value>
    </data>
    <data name="WaitlistBody" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>A countdown and a waitlist. Every sign-up is confirmed by email, bots are turned away without a word, and each visitor gets a few tries.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="PagesTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>More than one page</value>
    </data>
    <data name="PagesBody" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Each sample has the pages its business needs, like {0}'s shops with their opening hours. Every page has its own title, description and preview image.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LaunchTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>{0}, launched one platform at a time</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LaunchBody" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>The App Store for iPhone, a waitlist for Android and an install button for the web, all on one page. Installed, each sample opens as an app of its own.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LanguagesTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Two languages, two themes</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LanguagesBody" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Every page comes in English and Persian, right to left included, and in light and dark. Switch localization off and the site is English only.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="SearchTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Ready for search engines</value>
    </data>
    <data name="SearchBody" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Every page is prerendered, so search engines and visitors get its text before any code runs, along with its canonical link, structured data and a place in the sitemap.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="YoursTitle" xml:space="preserve">
